    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1964792335478186264",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1964792335478186264",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1964792335478186264",
      "text": "[9:40PM] #Ogolonto #TrafficUpdate \n\nA good pace of vehicular movement is still being experienced from Haruno inward to Agric, Aunty Kenny, Idiroko, Ogoloto, Majindu, Orita Aje, and all the way to Itanwolo.\n\nThe return journey from Itanwolo back to Majindu is characterized by a steady movement, although a slow delay is observed when approaching Ogoloto Intersection, primarily due to traffic interchanges at Ogoloto Junction.\n\nMovement towards Aunty Kenny is presently good, but approaching Agric, traffic is slow yet steady, largely attributed to commercial activities and pedestrian crossings.\n\nConversely, the stretch from Agric down to Haruno is experiencing a smooth traffic flow.\n\nThe road segment from Ogoloto inward Obasekumade Ferry Terminal is good, although traffic becomes momentarily congested when approaching Ebute Police Post.\n\nHowever, from Ibese Roundabout all the way to Igbogbo, traffic is flowing smoothly in both inward and outward journeys.\n\nFurthermore, the stretch from Ebute inward to General Hospital, Ojogbe, is good, but traffic slows down when approaching Ita Elewa, primarily due to traffic interchanges, though the situation is presently manageable.\n\nAs of this moment, no impediments to traffic flow have been recorded, and personnel are strategically deployed on ground, actively working to maintain traffic order.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
